Chapter: BvtBankCall
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

  bbc-mob : Integer, Integer -> WorldObject
  bbc-mob (x) (y) = WorldObject { serial = 1, kind = 1, x = x, y = y, z = 0, graphic = 400, hue = 0, container = 0, amount = 1, health = 50 }
  bbc-map : WalkMap = WalkMap { x = 0, y = 0, width = 0, height = 0, land = 0, solids = 0, stride = 0 }
 Damian, 2026-10-09: a banker answers "bank" from 15 tiles, through walls. Answers a bit per check: 1 a call to a banker
 carries 15 tiles and a whisper 1, 2 a banker 15 tiles off hears it with no line to judge, 4 one 16 off does not, 8 a
 shopkeeper call still carries 4 and needs its line; 15 is all.
  bbc-checks : Integer -> Integer
  bbc-checks (unused) = let me = bbc-mob 1420 1700
    in (if ns-call-range 0 2 == 15 & ns-call-range 8 2 == 1 then 1 else 0)
      + (if ns-heard bbc-map 2 me (bbc-mob 1435 1700) (ns-call-range 0 2) then 2 else 0)
      + (if not (ns-heard bbc-map 2 me (bbc-mob 1436 1700) (ns-call-range 0 2)) then 4 else 0)
      + (if ns-call-range 0 1 == 4 then 8 else 0)
  bvt-bank-call : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-bank-call (unused) = act
    n <- bbc-checks 0
    bvt-check ("a banker answers a call for the bank from 15 tiles, through walls (code " & show n & ")") (n == 15)
  end
